  "label": "The worker on the left is mapped as 'someone' who had too much gas",
  "description": "The text 'someone had too much gas' is mapped onto the worker on the left, implying he is the person experiencing the mishap. The visual of the worker pointing and standing near industrial machinery is juxtaposed with the text to create an analogical mapping where the worker represents 'someone' in the anecdote. This mapping is part of the 'camp joke structure' where a mundane situation is humorously exaggerated using taboo humor.",
